# circleci_groups (Data Source)

Fetches every CircleCI group in an organization. Pagination is followed
internally, so the result covers every group rather than a single page. Use
[`circleci_group`](group) to fetch one group by id.

## Availability

| CircleCI Cloud | CircleCI Server |
|---|---|
| yes | **no** |

Groups require a `circleci` type (standalone) organization, so this is Cloud
only. A CircleCI Server installation is always a `github` type organization.

-> **Members are a separate data source** This data source reports the groups
themselves, not their members. Use
[`circleci_group_membership`](./group_membership) to read the members of one
group.

## Example Usage

```terraform
data "circleci_groups" "all" {
  organization_id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

# Look a group up by name, since the API addresses groups by id.
output "developers_group_id" {
  value = one([
    for group in data.circleci_groups.all.groups : group.id
    if group.name == "developers"
  ])
}
```

